From: Veron
Subject: [PATCH] cc_core: a compound assignment is an assignment

`*p += v` loaded the POINTER at the pointed-at type's width. For `int *p` that
is a four-byte SIGNED read of an eight-byte pointer, so the address stored
through was truncated and sign-extended:

    *p = 5     lea_rax,[rbp-8] / mov_rax,[rax]                8 bytes, correct
    *p += 5    lea_rax,[rbp-8] / movsx_rax,DWORD_PTR_[rax]    4 bytes, SIGNED

Same expression, two different loads, differing only by which operator follows
it. `is_assignment` at cc_core.c:1831 is `match("=")` and nothing else, so a
compound assignment fell through to the RVALUE branch -- which steps the type
down first and then loads, because that is what an rvalue read of `*p` wants.
The lvalue branch loads first, at the pointer's own width, which is what an
assignment target wants. Both orders are correct for their own case; the flag
selecting between them did not know about `+=`.

`is_compound_operator` was already computed on the very next line and already
consulted by the two guards above (1834, 1922). Only this branch was missed.

WHAT IT COST. tcc's find_field walks anonymous struct/union members and
accumulates the offset with

    *cumofs += s->c;                            tccgen.c:4153

so every recursive resolution stored through a truncated pointer. A designated
initializer naming a member of an anonymous struct -- `union U { struct { int
a, b; }; }; union U g = {.b = 8};` -- segfaulted mc-tcc at compile time, while
the same initializer written with braces was fine, because the braced form does
not take the recursive path. tests2/90_struct-init is the case; it went from
SIGSEGV to passing.

THE FAULT WAS NOT LAYOUT-SENSITIVE, which is what made it worth bisecting by
construct: eight filename lengths through tools/layout-sweep.sh all failed
identically, so the heap-roulette shape that cost two rounds on the realloc
corruption did not apply here and the reduction converged in two passes.

This is the same rule as zz8 and it is now the ninth copy of it found missing.
The structural fix argued for at the end of MICRO-C.md -- one function
answering "is this an lvalue" -- would have made all nine a single line.

---
diff --git a/cc_core.c b/cc_core.c
--- a/cc_core.c
+++ b/cc_core.c
@@ -1928,7 +1928,26 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	if(is_assignment)
+	/* A COMPOUND ASSIGNMENT IS AN ASSIGNMENT, and this is the copy of that
+	 * rule that did not know it. `is_assignment` above is `match("=")` only,
+	 * so `*p += v` fell through to the rvalue branch below -- which steps the
+	 * type DOWN and then loads at the pointed-at width. For `int *p` that
+	 * loaded the eight-byte pointer as a four-byte signed int:
+	 *
+	 *     *p = 5     lea_rax,[rbp-8] / mov_rax,[rax]                8 bytes
+	 *     *p += 5    lea_rax,[rbp-8] / movsx_rax,DWORD_PTR_[rax]    4, SIGNED
+	 *
+	 * The truncated pointer is then stored through, so any address above 2GB
+	 * or with bit 31 set becomes a wild write. tcc's find_field does exactly
+	 * this -- `*cumofs += s->c` -- which is why a designated initializer
+	 * naming a member of an ANONYMOUS struct segfaulted mc-tcc while the same
+	 * initializer written with braces was fine.
+	 *
+	 * The load-before-step order in this branch is what makes it right: an
+	 * lvalue wants the POINTER at the pointer's width; only an rvalue read
+	 * wants the pointed-at type. Same rule as zz8, and the copies still
+	 * disagree. */
+	if(is_assignment || is_compound_operator)
 	{
 		while (num_dereference > 0)
 		{
